External dependencies, runtime environments, tools and assets
-----------------------------------------------------------
Dependencies are not bundled in Diane's wheel. Their original license and
notice files must remain intact in any environment or aggregate distribution
that does include them. The root MIT identifier is not an aggregate license.
A lock record is not evidence that all platform-specific artifacts are shipped
or have identical notices. Models downloaded at runtime are separate assets.

The source checkout's docs/licensing/index.md links the exact scoped package
inventory, primary-source evidence, model/data terms, obligations and unresolved
gates. Consult it before redistributing a checkout, environment, executable,
container, model cache, dataset or generated results. This audit is not legal
